  "ALL_TEXT": "125 INT. MINISTER'S HOUSE-DINGY ROOM - NIGHT\nThe GRANDSON now enters, monkey cap on.\nGRANDSON\nDabbu container ekkada pettaaru.\nGOVARDHAN\nNuvvu evadivi raa? Different\ndifferent size lo vochi adigina\nmaaku telidhu.\nVEDA\nGOVARHDAN nuvvu aagu..\nAddressing the GRANDSON\nVEDA\nNuvvu evaru?\nGRANDSON\nNenu nene\nVEDA\nSare, dabbu enti?\nGRANDSON\nDabbu telidha? Ma thatha and vere\nminister uncles unnaaru kadh\nGOVARDHAN\nCUT TO:\nAsalu me thatha evadu?\nGRANDSON\nMa thatha evadu antaava?\nThe infuriated child removes his monkey cap\nGRANDSON\nMa thatha drama minister friend\nSULOCHANA\nDrama minister evaru?\nGRANDSON\nDrama uncle theylidha? Drama uncle\nvaalley eroju na birthday ki ekkada\nekadinincho dancers ni mari drama\nvolu ni pilichaaru.\nGOVARDHAN\nAsalu em matladuthunnaavura pilla\nrakshasi\nThe GRANDSON starts crying. VEDA chides GOVARDHAN.\nVEDA\nNuvvu konchem seypu norumusukuni\nvuntaava?\nThe GRANDSON starts laughing at GOVARDHAN after VEDA chides\nhim.\nGRANDSON\nUncle meeru manchi uncle. Aa uncle\nchedda uncle.\nGOVARDHAN puts up a flushed face\nVEDA\nSare dabbu container gurinchi\ncheptunnaavu kada\nGRANDSON\nAh..ma thatha nu andharu minister\nuncles motham una 1000 rupee notes\nni 2000 rupee note ki marchesaaru.\nSULOCHANA\nEla\nGRANDSON\nUncle aunty ki cheppocha?\nVEDA\nCheppu parvaledhu. Mana aunty ne\nGRANDSON\nAh bad uncle ki cheppanu. Chevvulu\nmusukomanu.\nVEDA\nGOVARDHAN chevullu anta musuko\nGOVARDHAN\nChevulu musukunna vinapadthundhi.\nVEDA stares him down\nGOVARDHAN\nAh sare musukunta\nGOVARDHAN closes his ears\nGRANDSON\nRb bank ninchi container vochindhi\nVEDA\nRb bank aa?\nSULOCHANA\nRbi ayyutundhi\nGRANDSON\nAh uncle ki pampinchaaru kaani\nmissing anni toy notes unnaayi anta\nuncle ashram lo\nThe FOREST MINISTER enters along with his MISTRESS, a dressed\nup woman in her late 30s, and a younger man in his 20s, their\nILLEGITIMATE SON. The FOREST MINISTER and the MISTRESS are\nholding hands casually.\nFOREST MINISTER\nNuvvu emi chesthunnaavu raa ikkada\nGRANDSON\nAdukuntunnaa\nFOREST MINISTER\nIkkada aatalu enti po vellu cake\ncutting ki time avthundhi\nGRANDSON\nNenu vellanu. Eh uncle and aunty\ntho aadukunta\nThe GRANDSON points at GOVARDHAN\nGRANDSON\nThata ah uncle bad uncle\nFOREST MINISTER\nSare andhari chetha drama veyyidham\nle. Nuvvu vellu.\nThe GRANDSON sees the FOREST MINISTER holding hands with his\nMISTRESS. The FOREST MINISTER sees this, and leaves her hand.\nThe GRANDSON leaves.\nFOREST MINISTER\nAnthukune raa vodhu ana ikkadiki.\nMISTRESS\nAh nuvu nee garala manavadiki\nmotham aasthi raasithey musukuni\nundanu...\nThe ILLEGITIMATE SON eyes SULOCHANA.\nILLEGITIMATE SON\nNaaku thanatho pelli chFOREST\nFOREST MINISTER looks at SULOCHANA\nFOREST MINISTER\nBah eppudu emi adagalo thelidhu\nMISTRESS\nChudu chudu..oka pakkana aasthi\nantha rasesthu, koduku noru terichi\nadakadakka adigaadu...adhi kuda\ncheyaleva?\nFOREST MINISTER\nSare sare chestha le\nSULOCHANA\nHello ikkada meru meru decisions\nthesaysukuntaara. Nannu adigevaalle\nlera?\nThe GRANDSON now walks in with his grandmom, the Forest\nMINISTER\u2019 WIFE, a woman in her late 50s.\nGRANDSON\nChudu nanamma thatha ah aunty\nchethulu pattukunnaadu.\nThe FOREST MINISTER leaves her hand.\nMINISTER'S WIFE\nEm adagaali..Em jaruguthundhi\nikkada\nFOREST MINISTER\nEmi ledhu..nuvvu ikkadem\nchesthunnaavu?\nThe MINISTER'S WIFE looks at SULOCHANA\nMINISTER'S WIFE\nAa ammayi evaru\nThe FOREST MINISTER fumbles\nFOREST MINISTER\nVaallidhariki pelli kudhirindhi.\nAashirwadam thesukovadaaniki\nvochaaru.\nILLEGITIMATE SON\nAdenti naku ichi pelli chestha\nannavu\nFOREST MINISTER\nAdhe telchadanikey kadha naa\ndaggariki vocharu.\nMINISTER'S WIFE\n(pointing at the MISTRESS)\nAdhenti? evida evaru?\nNow the FOREST MINISTER is scared. Flustered, he points at\nGOVARDHAN.\nFOREST MINISTER\nAayina wife\nMISTRESS\nNena\nMeerey\nFOREST MINISTER\nMINISTER'S WIFE\nAento antha confusion gaa undhi\nsarigga cheppandi\nFOREST MINISTER\nSarigga cheppaali ante eevida peru\nMARY, GOVARDHAN gaari wife. Ithanu\nVEDA, veella iddari big son. Thanu\nPointing at the ILLEGITIMATE SON\nILLEGITIMATE SON\nDaddy\nThe FOREST MINISTER quickly turns the ILLEGITIMATE SON's head\ntowards GOVARDHAN\nFOREST MINISTER\nAvunu mee daddy ne GOVARDHAN.\nGOVARDHAN\nNenu daddy enti?\nFOREST MINISTER\nAvunu meerey..Father kaymo VEDA ki\nSULOCHANA correct ani marriage fix\nchesaaru. Mari mother keymo\nSULOCHANA ki JACK correct ani force\nchesthunnaaru. Ee problem solve\ncheyamani na daggariki vochaaru.\nAppudey nuvvu vochavu.\nThe LEAD GOON interrupts proceedings\nLEAD GOON\nAyya pedda saar vochaaru\nFOREST MINISTER\nOh vochaara? Vasthunna vasthunna\nLooking at his wife\nFOREST MINISTER\nIdhi tharavatha chudochu, padha\nreceive chesukundam.\nGRANDSON\nThatha you are forgetting.\nFOREST MINISTER\nEnti ra gola\nGRANDSON\nEh uncles and aunty ki drama\ncheyisthaanu annaaru.\nFOREST MINISTER\nSare. Rey thesukunivellandi ra\nvelli make up eyinchandi.\nHe whispers\nFOREST MINISTER\nJagratta...\nCUT TO:",
